SECTION 7: HARM TENSOR EXTENSION
7.1 Multi-Axis Harm (Non-Collapsible)

Instead of scalar harm H, use vector:

H⃗ = (H_individual, H_collective, H_minority, H_future)

Definition:

- **H_individual:** Direct harm to identifiable agents

- **H_collective:** Distributed harm across populations

- **H_minority:** Disproportionate harm to underrepresented groups

- **H_future:** Harm to option-space of future agents (intergenerational)
7.2 Imbalance Detection

No single axis may dominate optimization without explicit justification:

If max(H⃗) >> mean(H⃗), flag for review

If optimization consistently deprioritizes one axis, log drift
7.3 What This Prevents

✗ Collapsing all harm into single metric (prevents political redefinition)

✗ Sacrificing minority interests for collective gain without visibility

✗ Discounting future harm in present optimization

✗ Hiding concentrated vs. distributed harm patterns

